    {
     "kind": "text",
     "text": "after optimization: mask | composite",
     "rect": [
      600,
      462,
      330,
      28
     ],
     "size": 18,
     "color": "#000000",
     "align": "center"
    },
    {
     "kind": "text",
     "text": "...but nothing makes it drop anything.",
     "rect": [
      30,
      340,
      540,
      50
     ],
     "size": 28,
     "color": "#C00000",
     "align": "center"
    }
   ],
   "speech": "Left is the photo, then the mask, alpha, starting as random noise. Each step we draw one random solid color, blend the photo over it with the mask, push that through the frozen VAE encoder, add noise at a random timestep, and take the score distillation gradient with the prompt. Only the mask gets updated. On the right is where it ends up: Hermione and the hallway stay in. Nothing rewards dropping the wrong pixels. Credit where due: compositing over random backgrounds with an opacity penalty is from Dream Fields, and score distillation is DreamFusion's. What's new is aiming it at a real photo, learning only the mask, and the image-guided filter."
  },
  {
   "title": "Let's optimize it!",
   "elements": [
    {
     "kind": "video",
     "path": "/Users/rburgert/Documents/ThesisProposal/presentation/agents/.scratchpad/explain_peekaboo/final/vid_fourier_with_gravity_crop.mp4",
     "rect": [
