     "color": "#C00000"
    },
    {
     "kind": "text",
     "text": "+ bilateral filter",
     "rect": [
      30,
      410,
      540,
      50
     ],
     "size": 32,
     "color": "#C00000",
     "align": "center"
    }
   ],
   "speech": "The fix is a bilateral filter. We still learn every pixel of the mask, but every step the raw mask goes through a blur guided by the photo's colors, then a sigmoid. It's inside the forward pass, not post-processing, so similar colors get pulled to similar alpha and the edges follow the image. On VOC-C, our cropped single-object subset of Pascal VOC, that takes us from 0.34 to 0.52 mIoU. Not perfect, though: see the holes at the glasses and the tie, and the halo around his hair."
  },
